/-!
# Bender--Glauberman Section 14: sigma decompositions and maximal-group types

This file ports `BGsection14.v`, lines 65--455.  It introduces the
sigma-decomposition of an element, the two Feit--Thompson signalizer
subgroups, the set `kappa(M)`, and the four preliminary classes of maximal
subgroups.  It then ports the elementary facts through
`notP1type_Msigma_nil`, immediately before `Ptype_structure`.

MathComp's `x.`_pi` is represented by the unique factor of `x` whose order
is a `pi`-number.  The complementary factor is kept explicit.  Numerical
rank statements are expressed with `HasElementaryAbelianRankAtLeast`, as in
Sections 10--13 of this port.  Set cardinalities use `Set.ncard`.
-/

